{"id": "en-70147afc-0042", "text": "The profiler points at the serializer. However, there is also a compression stage that runs after it, and that stage is where the missing milliseconds are really hiding under load.  The change is small and the rollback is one command, so there is no reason to rush it.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 48, "topic_id": "en-however-additional", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "70147afc-5d29-417b-86a6-0982c251b6af", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "however", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-70147afc-0043", "text": "The iterator is lazy but also safe to reuse, because it wraps an immutable source and keeps its own cursor. Learners often assume it mutates state, but it never does here.", "has_turn": false, "first_turn_pos": -1, "scenario": "teaching", "turn_type": "none", "is_negative": true, "lang": "en", "word_count": 31, "topic_id": "en-but-also", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "70147afc-5d29-417b-86a6-0982c251b6af", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": "but", "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
